comments.body:
Thinking about extending to other types (and ranges). My feeling is that we want to keep only one list of settings (`SubscribePossibleSettingOptions`), and therefore we want to keep `Setting` and `Option`.

What about modifying `Option` to something like:

```proto
message Option {
    string option_value = 1;
    string option_description = 2;
}
```

Without specifying the type on the client side (so the client sets a string). The parsing has to be done on the camera side, and can return a `WRONG_ARGUMENT`.

Then, `SettingOptions` has to allow for ranges:

```proto
message SettingOptions {
    string setting_id = 1;
    string setting_description = 2;
    repeated Option options = 3;
    bool is_range = 4;
}
```

If `is_range == true`, then `repeated Option options` must contain exactly 2 options with `option_value` set respectively to [min, max].

I believe we also want to specify a reasonable interval for a range, and possibly a type, right?

